---
/**
 * /adms/support
 *
 * How to get help with ADMS. Content ported from the earlier
 * adapdev-adms-site support page.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Button from '../components/ui/Button.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Support — ADMS"
  description="How to get help with ADMS: email support, release notes, security disclosures, on-site onboarding and offline documentation."
>
  <section class="support">
    <p class="t-eyebrow">Support</p>
    <h1 class="t-h1 balance">The person who ships it answers the ticket.</h1>
    <p class="t-body-m balance lede">
      ADMS is maintained by Adapdev directly. When something breaks, the person who fixes it is the person who shipped it.
    </p>

    <div class="actions">
      <Button href="/contact">Contact support</Button>
      <Button href="/adms/release-notes" variant="ghost">Release notes</Button>
    </div>

    <article class="block">
      <h2 class="t-h3">Email support</h2>
      <p class="t-body-m">
        For general questions, bug reports and feature requests, email support via the Adapdev <a href="/contact">contact form</a>. Expect a reply within one Australian business day (Monday to Friday, Eastern time).
      </p>
      <p class="t-body-m">
        When reporting a bug, please include your ADMS version (<em>Help → About</em> in the desktop client, or the <code>Server-Version</code> response header from the API), the operating system, and the sequence of actions that produced the issue.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="block">
      <h2 class="t-h3">Release notes and updates</h2>
      <p class="t-body-m">
        Every ADMS release is documented in the <a href="/adms/release-notes">release notes</a>. The <a href="/adms/release-notes/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> is the recommended way to be notified of a new release without being on anyone's mailing list.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="block">
      <h2 class="t-h3">Security disclosures</h2>
      <p class="t-body-m">
        Found a security issue? Please report it privately via the <a href="/contact">contact form</a> with "SECURITY" in the subject line, rather than opening a public GitHub issue. We follow a responsible-disclosure process in line with the Australian Notifiable Data Breaches scheme; see our incident-response procedure for timing and detail.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="block">
      <h2 class="t-h3">On-site assistance (law firms, metro AU)</h2>
      <p class="t-body-m">
        For law-firm customers in metropolitan Australia, on-site onboarding and incident response are available. Travel is charged separately; see the <a href="/adms/pricing">pricing page</a> for the base tier or <a href="/contact">get in touch</a> for a quote.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="block">
      <h2 class="t-h3">Documentation</h2>
      <p class="t-body-m">
        Searchable product documentation is coming to this site. In the meantime, the ADMS installer ships with an offline operations manual (<code>%ProgramFiles%\Adapdev\ADMS\docs</code>) covering installation, backup, restore, rotation of signing keys, and the incident-response runbook.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .support {
    width: 100%; max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 100px 20px;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px;
  }
  .support h1 { max-width: 760px; }
  .lede { max-width: 720px; }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; padding-block: 4px 24px; }

  .block {
    padding: 24px;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--grey-20);
    border-radius: 12px;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px;
  }
  .block h2 { color: var(--white); }
  .block p { color: var(--grey); }
  .block a { color: var(--accent-sky); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .block a:hover, .block a:focus-visible { color: var(--white); }
  .block code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    padding: 1px 6px;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 809.98px) {
    .support { padding: 64px 20px; }
  }
</style>
